vectors/jsontestsuite: the JSONTestSuite parsing corpus (y_, n_, i_ files, 318), vendored unchanged.
Source:  https://github.com/nst/JSONTestSuite, directory test_parsing
Commit:  1ef36fa01286573e846ac449e8683f8833c5b26a
Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2016 Nicolas Seriot (vectors/jsontestsuite/LICENSE)
Expectations: y_ must parse, n_ must be rejected, i_ per the strict policy (docs/decisions/0001-vbm-json.md section 5), one line with a reason each in
vectors/jsontestsuite/i-verdicts.txt. `lake exe vbm-json-vectors --check` (part of Tier 1) runs every file through the reference and parseFast: both must agree
(verdict, error code, value) and match the expectation; the run also proves it can fail (all expectations flipped must all fail, mutants must differ).
Other vector sets are generated by that executable (LeanJson/Vectors.lean).
The written `vectors.jsonl` also carries the 318 files as set `jts` (the reference's verdict and canonical form on each file's bytes), so the C ABI test and every binding run them too.
